{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "toplevel_ref_metaparameter_axis",
    "description": "Conformance pin for the \u00a74.7 edge pipeline at a top-level models.<k> {ref}. Mounts toplevel_ref_metaparameter_axis_lib.esm, whose only axis is sized by the LEAF's own metaparameter (NLEV, default 4). \u00a74.7 \"Two mount forms, one mechanism\" forbids the two attachment points from differing, and the edge pipeline's step (1) resolves the referenced document in its OWN scope, so the leaf's metaparameters close and fold AT THE MOUNT (\u00a79.7.6 site 3) and `lev` reaches the importing registry as size 4 \u2014 the importer redeclares nothing, which is \u00a79.7.5's \"without redeclaring them\". All three bindings that mount a top-level {ref} \u2014 Python, Rust and (since 2026-09-11) Julia \u2014 do this, so this is a 3-of-3 pin. It lives under tests/fixtures/ rather than tests/valid/ because TypeScript and Go do not mount a top-level {ref} at all and the corpus sweep would score them a false pass.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciAST"],
    "created": "2026-09-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": ["subsystem", "index_sets", "metaparameter", "mount", "toplevel-ref", "regression"]
  },
  "models": {
    "M": { "ref": "./toplevel_ref_metaparameter_axis_lib.esm" }
  }
}
